<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Läänemaa</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1224 CE (approx.) · capital Lihula</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Coastal county of western Estonia, centred on Lihula, which became the mainland core of the Bishopric of Ösel-Wiek.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Läänemaa, known in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> as Rotalia or Maritima, covered the western coast of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia">Estonia</a> facing the islands of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saaremaa">Saaremaa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiiumaa">Hiiumaa</a>. Its main stronghold was at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lihula">Lihula</a>, and the area had close ties with the islanders across the narrow straits.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its elders led farming and fishing communities on the low coastal land. In 1220 a Swedish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-of-sweden">King John I</a> occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lihula">Lihula</a>, but the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/saaremaa">Oeselians</a> attacked and wiped out the garrison, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden's</a> first attempt to gain a foothold in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia">Estonia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Läänemaa was subdued by the Germans and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> by 1224 and became the mainland part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bishopric-of-osel-wiek">Bishopric of Ösel-Wiek</a>, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> first resided at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lihula">Lihula</a> and later at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haapsalu">Haapsalu</a> (Hapsal). The name survives in Lääne county.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/laanemaa.jpg" alt="Läänemaa" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Kalev35 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Allikaj%C3%A4rve_l%C3%B5kkekoht.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1224 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Lihula</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Estonian paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Estonian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/estonia">Estonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Rotalia, Maritima, Wiek</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1012&amp;focus=laanemaa" aria-label="Läänemaa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5182 194 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Läänemaa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5502 450L5479 467"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5479 467h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5502 450h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5502 450h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1012&amp;focus=laanemaa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
